+
+**The defect** (`vmedefaultkill`, HIGH).  `DEVICE_ACCESS(vme)` named ten offsets of its 4 KiB window; every other offset
+reached `default:`, which printed with `debug()` -- silent at default verbosity while free-running -- and called
+`exit(1)`, so the emulator ended with no visible reason.  The device exists only on `-E mvme88k -e mvme187` (window
+0xfff40000-0xfff40fff).  The OpenBSD 2.2 mvme88k driver's attach reads MASTERCTL and writes MASTERCTL, MASTER3, MASTER4
+and MASTER4MOD -- four of the unimplemented registers -- so on HEAD that guest's attach would end the emulator at its
+first MASTERCTL read (read from the driver source; the witness measures the access sites, not a boot).  Witness, rung 3
+on unmodified `-E mvme88k -e mvme187` at HEAD 5dbc000e: 7 of 7 guest access sites end the emulator (rc 1), and a
+free-running MASTERCTL read dies with no `[ vme:` text (`regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/witness_20261020/SUMMARY.md`).
